@layout DefaultLayout
@page "/portfolio/entities"

@{
	var canonicalUrl = "https://fydar.dev/portfolio/entities";
	void PageMetadata(IMetadataFactory factory)
	{
		factory.UseTitle("Entities - Fydar");
		factory.UseDescription("A complete entities system.");
		factory.UseCanonicalUrl(canonicalUrl);
		factory.UseImage(image =>
		{
			image.Url = "https://fydar.dev/media/header.webp";
			image.Alt = "A portrait of Fydar in an anime art style.";
		});
	}
	var breadcrumbs = new BreadcrumbList()
	{
		new BreadcrumbListItem("Portfolio", "https://fydar.dev/portfolio"),
		new BreadcrumbListItem("Entities", "https://fydar.dev/portfolio/entities"),
	};
}

<HeadFragment>
	<MetadataComponent Metadata="@PageMetadata" />
	<BreadcrumbListComponent Model="@breadcrumbs" />
</HeadFragment>

<article class="page-entities">

    <div class="container">
        <Block_ArticleHeader>
            <h1 data-nosnippet>Entities</h1>
        </Block_ArticleHeader>

        <Block_ArticleIntroduction>
            <Sidebar>
                <Block_PillCloud>
                    <Pill_CSharp />
                </Block_PillCloud>

                <p>A complete entities system.</p>

                <menu class="externallinks" aria-label="Project External links">
                </menu>

                <ShareLink Url="@canonicalUrl" />
            </Sidebar>
            <Container>
            </Container>
        </Block_ArticleIntroduction>

        <Block_ArticleOutlined>
            <Sidebar>
                <aside>
                    <Block_TableOfContents />
                </aside>
            </Sidebar>
            <Content>

                <OutlineSection Id="ecs" LinkName="Entity Component System">
                    <Block_ArticleHeading>
                        <hgroup>
                            <p>Designing the</p>
                            <h2>Entity Component System</h2>
                        </hgroup>
                    </Block_ArticleHeading>

                    <p>I went about designing my own ECS. Firstly, I laid out my requirements for the ECS.</p>

                    <ul>
                        <li>I want it to be <b>hierarchical</b>.</li>
                        <li>I want parent-child relationships to be <b>hard-typed</b>.</li>
                        <li>I want to take advantage of the <b>latest C# APIs</b> to achieve maximum performance.</li>
                        <li>I want to use <b>zero reflection</b> to ensure maximum linkability and performance.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h3>Hard-Typed Relationships</h3>

                    <p>I wanted to bring <b>natural object-oriented data structures</b> into the realm of <b>ECS</b>. To do this, I started by introducing <b>Entity Archetypes</b>, which allowed me to specify archetypes of entities that always contain set components. I didn't want to loose the flexibility of a traditional ECS, so I made sparse components an optional feature of the archetypes.</p>

                    <p>I then experimented with what it might look like to add <b>parent-child relationships</b> to the archetypes, but I found myself blurring the lines between what is an entity and what is a component. It was clear that this wasn't the solution I was looking for, so I continued experimenting...</p>

                    <p>Eventually I explored replacing both entities and components with a single entry in the hierarchy: thus creating the <b>Node</b>. This is somewhat similar to what Godot does, however the hard-typed relationships between parent and children nodes in Godot starts and ends with 2D, 3D, and UI nodes. What if I took the hard-typed scene root nodes and brought it to every node in the scene?</p>
                </OutlineSection>

                <OutlineSection Id="entities" LinkName="Entity Definition API">
                    <Block_ArticleHeading>
                        <hgroup>
                            <p>Designing the</p>
                            <h2>Entity Definition API</h2>
                        </hgroup>
                    </Block_ArticleHeading>

                    <Block_Callout Type="construction">
                        <Icon><SvgSprite Link="/icons.svg?v=1#fluent-emoji-high-contrast--construction" Alt="Check" /></Icon>
                        <ChildContent>This section of my website is currently <b>under construction</b>.</ChildContent>
                    </Block_Callout>

                </OutlineSection>

            </Content>
        </Block_ArticleOutlined>
    </div>
</article>
